# {{ titleCase (sentenceCase name) }}

> A short description of this package...

{{#if compiled}}
A **compiled** package. It ships `dist`, built by `pnpm build`; turbo builds it before anything that depends on
it. TypeScript, vitest and the dev servers read its `src` through the `development` condition, so none of them
need a build first.
{{else}}
A **JIT** package. It ships TypeScript source, and every consumer compiles it: Vite, rspack and vitest. Node
can't run it directly, so a Node app has to bundle it.
{{/if}}

## Installation

```sh
pnpm -F <your-workspace> add @example/{{ name }} --workspace
```

## Imports

Import this package's own modules through its `imports` map instead of relative paths. Specifiers have no
extension; `.ts` and `.tsx` files both resolve:

```ts
import { something } from '#some/module'; // src/some/module.ts
import { Component } from '#some/Component'; // src/some/Component.tsx
```
{{#if compiled}}

Import files, not directories: in `dist`, `#some` only resolves to `dist/some.js`.
{{/if}}
